<Text>setdisplayunit(&apos;PRI&apos;, &apos;&apos;)&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(&apos;Pulsewidth&apos;, &apos;&apos;)&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(&apos;Bandwidth&apos;, &apos;&apos;)&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(&apos;fs&apos;, &apos;&apos;)&#x000D;&#x000A;setdisplayunit(&apos;fc&apos;, &apos;&apos;)&#x000D;&#x000A;%The equation line(s) above have been added by the conversion tool to un-associate the variable&#x2019;s unit, so that the variable is interpreted the same way as the previous release.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;PRI_Sample_Num = PRI * fs;&#x000D;&#x000A;CPI_Num = 32;&#x000D;&#x000A;SigPow = 1e-6;&#x000D;&#x000A;% PRI_Input=tune(100);&#x000D;&#x000A;% Pulse_Width=tune(10);&#x000D;&#x000A;%Bandwidth=tune(2e6);&#x000D;&#x000A;% PRI = 200e-6;&#x000D;&#x000A;%PulseWidth = 10e-6;&#x000D;&#x000A;%Pulsewidth = PulseWidth;&#x000D;&#x000A;NumberOfAnt=tune(16);&#x000D;&#x000A;%Pulsewidth = PulseWidth;&#x000D;&#x000A;NumberOfAnt1D = NumberOfAnt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;SignalClutterRatio=tune(-14);  % signal-to-clutter ratio (dB)&#x000D;&#x000A;SCR = SignalClutterRatio;&#x000D;&#x000A;PlatformVt=tune(0);&#x000D;&#x000A;TargetVt=tune(116);&#x000D;&#x000A;VT = PlatformVt;&#x000D;&#x000A;TVt = TargetVt;&#x000D;&#x000A;SNR = 10;  % signal-to-noise ratio(dB)</Text>
<UnitUse><T>Int</T><D>2</D></UnitUse>
