SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Simulation Task&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;This workspace as a template shows how to set up the arbitrary type radar simulation based on the generalized framework and how to generate the echoes from the scatters of targets.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Workspace Description&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;SystemVue has 88 models and 70 templates to cover all advanced radar system designs.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;To design your own system, you don&apos;t have to start from scratch.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;SystemVue &lt;B&gt;provides uniform processes &lt;/B&gt;for designing and testing Radar systems using preconfigured simulation templates.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Users can begin by modifying a similar template to their system based on their system spec.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Additionally, your legacy IP in&amp;nbsp;m code&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: red; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;or C/C++ code can be imported to SystemVue as SystemVue models, or save it in your own library and use it in conjunction with existing SystemVue models.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;This workspace as a template shows how to set up the arbitrary type radar simulation based on the generalized framework and how to generate the echoes from the scatters of targets.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;The example includes three layers: trajectory layer, antenna layer&amp;nbsp;and signal layer. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;In the trajectory layer, the RADAR_Platform model and RADAR_TargetScatterLocation model are used to generate the trajectories of transmitter, receiver, and scatters of target. The output is at the ECI frame(x, y, z). &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;In antenna layer, the transmitter antenna gains and the receiver antenna gains to the scatters of targets can be computed according to the locations of transmitter platforms and receiver platforms and scatters of targets. The locations are at the ECI frame.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;In the signal layer, the input signal will be changed to the echoes from different scatters of targets according to the locations at ECI frame at each sampling time and the antenna gains from antenna layer. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The RADAR_Platform model and RADAR_TargetScatterLocation model support two types of trajectory generation:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&#x00B7;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;User defined file import (Parameter Trajectory_Mode = 1: User Defined) &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The file format is (x, y, z) in the ECI frame. Each line is the position value at each time step.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&#x00B7;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Real time computation (Parameter Trajectory_Mode = 0: Cartesian )&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The initial positions of platform and target are set with the parameter Position_Initial in the geodetic system (Longitude(degree), Latitude(degree), Height(meters)).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;If the platform is not static, the Velocity_Initial and Accelerate_Initial parameters can be used to set the initial velocity (m/s) and accelerate (m/s&lt;SUP&gt;2&lt;/SUP&gt;) in the body frame. The random value of jerk can be provided when IsRondomError = true.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;The input roll, pitch and yaw angles are the Euler angles which are three angles introduced by Euler to describe the orientation of a rigid body. Although the relative orientation between any two Cartesian frames can be described by Euler angles, this model is focused merely on the transformation between the vehicle-carried (or the local) NED and the body frames, following a particular rotation sequence. More specifically, the adopted Euler angles move the reference frame to the referred frame, following a Z-Y-X (or the so-called 3&#x2013;2&#x2013;1) rotation sequence. These three Euler angles are also known as the yaw (or heading), pitch, and roll angles.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To run the template, please execute the following steps.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 0pt 0.25in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Open the workspace and observe the main design (design2). &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 0pt 0.25in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;General Setup for moving platform simulation is considered in three layers.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 0pt 0.25in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;a.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The Trajectory Layer with green color is to set Tx and Rx moving property.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Also the target moving properties with initial range, velocity, position are set here. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 0pt 0.25in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;b.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The Antenna layer with green color is for setting the position of Tx and Rx array antennas.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in 0pt 0.25in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;c.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 7pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; COLOR: black; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The signal layer includes sub-Systems, Transmitter, Beamformer , Array Atenna, Environments, RF Receiver, Signal processor and measurements.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;b. Key parameters defined using slides for easy to use &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;2. Run the simulation by click on the &apos;Run Analysis&apos; button in the first row of Manu bars.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;Then you can observe the simulation results.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&apos;&gt;Look the bottom row. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 1, LFM transmission signal is shown.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 2, the received signal is hidden into the strong Clutter and noise.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 3, through MTI and MTD the pulse is recovered and detected.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;In Figure 4, the signal at the CFAR output is cleaned up.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Two 3D plots are shown in the design page to show the Detected signal in the Range-Doppler plane.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The first one shows the detected signal under the condition of without MTI.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The second one is for with MTI.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-spacerun: yes&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;4. Modify Key parameters by using slides to observe the results to know the system works Ok or not.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;To create your own system you can modify the template by changing parameters or replace models that are either in the radar library or import your models in the design.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
